Are you ready to take ownership, problem solve and keep our payroll operations running with precision? We have an opportunity for a Senior Payroll Specialist to join our team!&nbsp; &nbsp;

Reporting to the Director, Global Payroll, t he Sr Payroll Specialist is responsible for executing accurate and compliant payrolls across multiple jurisdictions. The role requires strong analytical skills, technical understanding of payroll systems (ADP, SAP), and a focus on continuous improvement. This position ensures payroll accuracy, compliance with regulations, and seamless employee experience, supporting Hasbro’s global payroll transformation objectives. The role acts as a bridge between operations and management, collaborating closely with payroll team members and driving continuous process improvement. &nbsp;

This role will co-manage 5 pay groups (2 biweekly hourly, 2 biweekly salary, and 1 monthly) in ADP Vantage, &amp; eTime, while supporting the implementation of ADP GlobalView and Workforce Manager. This is a critical, high-visibility role, and we are seeking the best candidate to bring their expertise of payroll, tax, compliance, and innovative, tech-driven payroll processes. &nbsp;

Effective from the date that Hasbro opens its new Boston location, this position will be onsite Tuesday - Thursday at Hasbro’s new HQ location in Boston, MA. In the interim, this position will be onsite Tuesday -Thursday at Hasbro’s HQ in Pawtucket, RI or at Hasbro’s temporary location in Boston, MA. &nbsp;

 

A day in the life:

• Manage multi-state processing and reporting, including state tax registrations, withholding accounts, and unemployment accounts. &nbsp;

• Maintain payroll system accuracy, including earnings codes, deductions, tax configurations, and pay rules. &nbsp;

• Process and validate payroll results, balancing gross-to-net calculations, reconciliations, and audit trails. &nbsp;

• Review and analyze employee master data, time and attendance, and variable pay inputs for correctness. &nbsp;

• Reconcile payroll results, support general ledger accuracy, and identify discrepancies. &nbsp;

• Support payroll close, tax filings, and year-end reporting.&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Manage payroll inquiries through effective communication and resolution. &nbsp;

• Collaborate cross-functionally with HRIS, HR Operations, and Finance to maintain data accuracy. &nbsp;

• Serve as an SME for system functionality, upgrades, and cross-functional process enhancements. &nbsp;

• Develop, maintain, and implement policies and standard operating procedures to ensure compliance with internal controls &nbsp;

• Lead payroll audits and internal control testing, ensuring compliance with SOX requirements.

